            <ArticleTitle>Neonatal pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-116</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0146-0005(16)30116-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.semperi.2016.11.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain management in the neonatal ICU remains challenging for many clinicians and in many complex care circumstances. The authors review general pain management principles and address the use of pain scales, non-pharmacologic management, and various agents that may be useful in general neonatal practice, procedurally, or at the end of life. Chronic pain and neonatal abstinence are also noted.</AbstractText>
